 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Animated Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an animated landing page?\", \"a\": \"An animated landing page is a single page with one goal, such as a signup or a demo request, that uses motion to make a point. Steps slide in on scroll, a counter climbs, or a short product loop plays. The offer still reads clearly with every animation switched off.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an animated landing page?\", \"a\": \"List each animation with its job and its length, and keep the headline and main button still. Then describe the page to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder'>AI landing page builder</a>, which builds it from that prompt, motion included. Before you publish, load it with reduced motion turned on and send a test through every form.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does landing page animation slow down the page?\", \"a\": \"It can, depending on what you animate. web.dev notes that an animation that moves an element using something other than transform is likely to be slow. Slide elements with transform, fade them with opacity, and compress any video loop before it goes on the page.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I look for in animated landing page examples?\", \"a\": \"Look at when each animation starts and stops, not only how it looks. Scroll each example slowly, then fast, and check that the text reads at both speeds. Then reload it with the reduce motion setting on. If a product needs a minute of motion to explain, study a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/video'>video landing page</a> instead of a long loop.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should animated landing pages play their animations automatically?\", \"a\": \"Short ones can; long ones need a control. Under WCAG 2.2.2, motion that starts automatically, lasts more than 5 seconds, and plays in parallel with other content needs a pause, stop, or hide control. A counter that finishes in 2 seconds needs nothing extra. A product loop that keeps going needs a pause button.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which landing page animation examples are worth copying?\", \"a\": \"Copy the ones that explain something. A scroll reveal suits a process in 3 steps, a counter suits a running total, and a short loop suits a product doing its main task. Skip motion that only decorates, such as a spinning logo or a headline that types itself out letter by letter.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does a landing page with animation work the same on a phone?\", \"a\": \"Not entirely. A phone has no cursor to rest on a card, and a hover effect there fires only on a tap, if at all. Trigger it on scroll or tap instead. Test on a real phone as well: a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/mobile'>mobile landing page</a> is read one screen at a time, and every animation competes for that small space.\"}, {\"q\": \"What code makes landing page animations start on scroll?\", \"a\": \"The Intersection Observer API lets the page observe when an element starts to intersect the viewport, the part of the page on screen. At that moment the page adds a class, and the element slides or fades in. Emergent writes that code from your prompt, and paid plans export it to your GitHub repository.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many animations should an animated landing page have?\", \"a\": \"As few as have a job: at most one per section, and none on the headline or the main button. If two things move on the same screen at once, cut one. Count them before you publish; on a long page, four is plenty.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an animated landing page include a signup form with steps?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/multi-step'>multi step form</a> fits an animated landing page well: each step slides in after the last answer, and a progress bar fills as the visitor goes. Emergent builds conversational flows with one question per screen, and every answer saves to a database you own.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
  "alpb---prompt": "<p>Build an animated landing page that saves every signup to a database I own.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build an animated landing page that saves every signup to a database I own.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Scroll Reveal\", \"add\": \"Add a scroll reveal that slides each step in as it enters the screen.\"}, {\"label\": \"Animated Counter\", \"add\": \"Add an animated counter that reads its total from the database.\"}, {\"label\": \"Demo Loop\", \"add\": \"Add a demo loop with a pause button that stops after 3 plays.\"}, {\"label\": \"Reduced Motion\", \"add\": \"Add a reduced motion version with a still hero and no carousel.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
